# Patch categories, used by --list and --category in the three scripts.
#
# Format: <category> <repo path prefix>
# A patch belongs to the category of the first prefix that matches its source
# project path (the directory it lives in). Unmatched projects fall back to
# "other" so nothing silently disappears from --list.
#
# The directory layout stays <repo path>/NNNN-<slug>.patch because that is what
# decides where a patch applies; the category is only a grouping for humans and
# for selective runs such as: check.sh --category camera

camera    hardware/interfaces
media     frameworks/av
# The cameraservice fence fix lives in frameworks/av but belongs to the camera
# work, so name it explicitly; a full patch path wins over a project prefix.
camera    frameworks/av/0005-cameraservice-close-acquire-fence-handles-in-passthr.patch
display   frameworks/native
wifi      hardware/broadcom/wlan
wifi      packages/modules/Wifi
wifi      packages/modules/Connectivity
system    frameworks/base
system    lineage-sdk
system    packages/apps
system    packages/modules/adb
system    packages/modules/IntentResolver
system    packages/services
power     bootable/recovery
build     build/make
build     system/core
build     system/sepolicy
build     prebuilts/gcc
build     vendor/lineage
